<p>Somali pirates hijacked a Togo-flagged oil tanker off Yemen on Saturday and forced it toward Somalia, according to accounts that cited Somali security officials, Yemen&#x27;s Coast Guard and maritime sources. HUM News English and GBC Ghana identified the vessel as the MT Eureka, and HUM News English said Somali authorities confirmed Sunday that the tanker had entered Somali waters. The seizure followed other recent attacks on ships near the Horn of Africa. Shabelle, carried by AllAfrica, described the Gulf of Aden incident as a second strike in weeks, while HUM News English described it as the third such abduction in recent weeks. The New York Times and The Straits Times said the attack&#x27;s location and timing raised concern about possible collaboration between Somali pirates and Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OkuBPKSibL1fvntvppY8gM2AjJ8CwNW23uzNYMPJDclkgGYAK0BKU6CiqWcf8XTSCsXoj47DTtzNuEfoiOMLlWEIYcWmbMc8-CRpmOfxbGlm_2jlTvl4WMnsqQZs-MuBrI4D8qCoWDG2B05JRHaZ4MPjwJetSDRt7EGc-MftO8DraK-b9mO2vkgb6OpiIp_hUEqNy4ribh7hm0DWgOSv86CiIKA_jw' alt='Maritime police forces from the Puntland region of Somalia patrolling the Gulf of Aden last year.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Mogadishu pressure: HUM News English described the hijacking as a significant embarrassment for the Somali government in Mogadishu.</li><li>Traffic shift: RFI, carried by AllAfrica, said increased traffic around the Horn of Africa and the diversion of naval forces during the Middle East war could create more openings for pirates.</li><li>Attention gap: De Volkskrant reported that Somali piracy activity was growing while international attention remained focused on the Houthis.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Yemen Coast Guard: Yemen&#x27;s Coast Guard placed the boarding in the Yemeni portion of the Gulf of Aden and at first described the assailants as unidentified individuals. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-and-diverted-to-somalia/'>HUM News English</a>)</li><li>Somali authorities: Somali authorities said they were monitoring the situation and working to recover the ship. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-and-diverted-to-somalia/'>HUM News English</a>)</li><li>Abshir Hashi Ali: The Galmudug State ports official said the tanker was being held for ransom off Puntland and its crew was detained. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-and-diverted-to-somalia/'>HUM News English</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/02/world/middleeast/hijacking-tanker-houthis-somalia-pirates.html'>Oil Tanker Hijacking Stokes Fear of Links Between Houthi Rebels and Somali Pirates</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/oil-tanker-hijacking-stokes-fears-of-new-disruption-in-gulf-region'>Oil tanker hijacking stokes fears of new disruption in Gulf region</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202605040063.html'>Somalia: Somali Pirates Hijack Oil Tanker in Gulf of Aden, Second Strike in Weeks</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-and-diverted-to-somalia/'>Oil tanker hijacked off Yemen coast and diverted to Somalia</a> - humenglish.com</li><li><a href='https://eastleighvoice.co.ke/somalia/343341/somalia-piracy-fears-resurface-after-wave-of-vessel-hijackings-off-key-shipping-route'>Somalia piracy fears resurface after wave of vessel hijackings off key shipping route</a> - eastleighvoice.co.ke</li><li><a href='https://www.gbcghanaonline.com/features/togo-flagged-oil-tanker-hijacked-off-coast-of-yemen-headed-towards-somalia/2026/'>Togo-flagged oil tanker hijacked off coast of Yemen, headed towards Somalia</a> - gbcghanaonline.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/russian/articles/c0r2ngz82y7o'>Нефтяной танкер был захвачен у берегов Йемена